NOTICE — third-party components used by ExLlamaV3ROCm
=======================================================

This repository contains the deployment glue, controller, launchers, server
engine integration and patches written for the two- and three-node Strix Halo rigs
(MIT, see LICENSE). It redistributes or references the following third-party
work; each component keeps its own license and attribution:

ExLlamaV3 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Turboderp)
  Used through the `anoane/exllamav3-anemone` fork (PR #449, branch `dsv41f`,
  base commit d45e89611738e9134f72f5c9679cc9eae113bba8) plus the local
  `multi-node-rocm` commit series in `patches/exllamav3/`.
  Source is fetched by `setup.sh`; nothing from it is vendored here.

Kyojin (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Turboderp)
  <https://github.com/Yamz-Labs/kyojin>, commit
  e2f37564bbae01a6ea8ad4176dfd97db09c253aa (release 1.8.2).
  The HTTP/chat/parser/test layer in `tools/ds41/` is vendored from Kyojin
  with per-file attribution headers; the full license text is retained at
  `tools/ds41/LICENSE.kyojin`. See `tools/ds41/README.md` for the file map
  and the two clearly marked LOCAL (exl3-tp) adaptations.

OdinLink-Five (kernel driver GPL-2.0; userspace library, RCCL/NCCL plugins,
  CLI, daemon and all other components MIT; Copyright (c) Geramy)
  <https://github.com/Geramy/OdinLink-Five>, upstream commit 4534f58 plus the
  local patch series in `patches/odinlink/` (driver, userspace library and
  RCCL v7 plugin; see its README). Only the patches are redistributed — the
  patched files of `driver/` are GPL-2.0 derivative work and must stay
  GPL-2.0; the library and RCCL plugin patches apply to MIT userspace code.
  Source is fetched by `setup.sh` and `odinlink-multilink/build.sh`.

Linux kernel, drivers/thunderbolt (GPL-2.0)
  `patches/linux/0001-thunderbolt-source-xdomain-protocol-handlers.patch`
  modifies `drivers/thunderbolt/` and `include/linux/thunderbolt.h`.
  `odinlink-multilink/build.sh` fetches the source of the distribution kernel
  it builds for (Fedora SRPM, kernel.org as a fallback), applies the patch and
  builds the module locally. Only the patch is redistributed; it and the
  module built from it are GPL-2.0.

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash reference encoding (MIT, DeepSeek-AI)
  `tools/ds41/testdata/reference/` carries the official reference
  implementation and golden test inputs/outputs used by the golden prompt
  tests (see `tools/ds41/README.md`).

Model weights and Engram tables (NOT redistributed in this repository)
  Quantized checkpoint: `LibertAIDAI/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2.9bpw`
  (EXL3 2.9 bpw quantization of DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017); for TP=3 also
  `LibertAIDAI/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-3.5bpw` (downloaded by hand,
  see README).
  Engram source tables: `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017`
  (shards model-00047/00048-of-00048.safetensors). Both are downloaded by
  `setup.sh` under their upstream licenses/terms; model data never enters
  git (see .gitignore).

AMD ROCm wheels and PyTorch (MIT/license of the ROCm software stack)
  `torch[device-gfx1151]==2.14.0+rocm10.1.0a20260822` and
  `rocm[devel,device-gfx1151]==10.1.0a20260822` from AMD's wheel index; see
  `requirements/rocm.txt` and `requirements/python.txt` for the exact pins.
